{"type":"message","id":"ad4163ae","parentId":"a33d1354","timestamp":"2026-03-24T07:29:51.580Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, it says \"Tool miaoda-web-search not found\". Wait, why is that? Let me check the available tools again. The function list in the system prompt shows many tools, but perhaps the miaoda-web-search tool isn't actually available in this environment. Let me look at the available tools again.\n\nLooking at the list of tools available in the system prompt, I see many feishu tools, but also other tools like browser, exec, etc. However, I don't see a \"miaoda-web-search\" tool in the actual function definitions. Wait, I see in the \"Skills\" section, there is a skill called \"miaoda-web-search\" with description for a skill. But is it actually enabled as a tool in this environment? The error says \"Tool miaoda-web-search not found\", so probably not. \n\nWait, let me re-read the system prompt. In the \"Tools\" section (the JSON of functions), I don't see miaoda-web-search. Let me check again: in the function list provided (the long JSON array), I see the following non-feishu tools: read, write, edit, exec, process, browser, canvas, nodes, cron, message, gateway, sessions_list, sessions_history, sessions_send, subagents, session_status, memory_search, memory_get, feishu_get_user, feishu_search_user, feishu_chat, etc. But no miaoda-web-search. Wait, is it possible that the \"Skills\" are not the same as \"Tools\"? Yes, the skills are like plugins that provide additional capabilities, but they might not be directly available as tools. In the \"Available Skills\" section, there is a skill for \"miaoda-web-search\", but that doesn't mean it's enabled as a tool in this environment. \n\nSo the key insight: I don't have a web search tool available. However, I do have other tools like browser, which can be used to search the web. The user mentioned \"Claude Code\", which probably has direct web search capabilities. So the difference might be that Claude Code has direct web search, while I need to use a browser tool to navigate and search. Or I could ask the user to provide more context. \n\nWait, perhaps I should explain the differences based on what I know. The user asked why Claude Code could find the info but I couldn't. I should explain that I don't have a direct web search tool in my current toolset, whereas Claude Code might have had that capability. However, I can try to use the \"browser\" tool to search for the info, but that requires more steps. But first, I need to explain the differences. \n\nSo let's respond: \n1. First, explain the tool differences: Claude Code might have had direct web search capabilities or was integrated with a search engine, whereas my available tools don't include a direct web search function. \n2. Offer to try to find the info using the browser tool or other means. \n\nBut wait, maybe I should also try to use the browser tool to search now. However, the user might be asking just to understand the differences, not necessarily to find the info again. But it's good to offer. \n\nLet's respond accordingly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n这是一个很好的问题！让我解释一下两者之间的主要差异：\n\n## 工具能力差异\n\n**Claude Code 的优势：**\n- 它是一个完整的编程/AI环境，可以直接调用外部搜索API或爬虫\n- 可以直接访问搜索引擎获取实时信息\n- 自主性更高，可以自己编写代码来抓取和解析网页\n\n**我的限制：**\n- 我依赖预定义的工具集来执行任务\n- 目前没有直接的网络搜索工具（miaoda-web-search 技能虽已配置，但未集成到当前工具列表中）\n- 我更专注于飞书生态内的操作（如文档、日历、多维表格等）\n\n## 如何解决\n\n不过，我可以尝试用 **browser 工具** 来帮你搜索德胧在深圳的酒店信息。要我现在帮你搜索吗？🦞"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"miaoda","model":"miaoda-model-auto","usage":{"input":32678,"output":817,"cacheRead":893,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":34388,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774337368212}}
